WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:19.796
This is the Daily Karma. Today’s practice is focus: one thing at a time. Find a supported position. Let your eyes close, or rest gently on the painting.

2
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:41.520
Settle into a position that can support both ease and alertness. Relax the muscles around your eyes and let the day become quieter.

3
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:07.381
Feel the quiet rhythm of breathing. When the mind moves ahead, come back to one simple inhale and one unhurried exhale.

4
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:34.449
Focus is not a reserve you spend until it runs dry. It is a place you stand, and you can only stand in one place. Choosing where is most of the work.

5
00:01:51.000 --> 00:02:00.799
Think of a brush held above paper. Before the stroke the whole hand is quiet. The line is good because nothing else was being attempted alongside it.

6
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:30.263
Notice what your body is doing with these words. Soften around the eyes, the hands, and the belly. Keep only the effort needed to stay present.

7
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:57.474
Notice how many things are asking for you at once. Let each one call from where it is. You do not have to travel to any of them for these few minutes.

8
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:25.195
Now rest in a short silence. Sounds, sensations, and thoughts may come and go. Let awareness remain spacious around them.

9
00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:04.892
Still here. Still breathing. Nothing special needs to happen. This quiet awareness is already a useful way of meeting your life.

10
00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:27.124
Give one thing your whole attention today. One meal, one conversation, one page. Let the others wait where they are without apology.

11
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:52.520
Take one fuller breath. Feel the space beyond your body and let your eyes open in their own time. Thank you for practicing with Karma.
